lty of Health Sciences & Medicine Faculty of Law Faculty of Society & Design Transformation CoLab Academic calendar Census dates Manage your enrolment Subject finder Timetables Enrol in your subjects Changing your subjects Changing your program Withdrawing or taking a break Compassionate or compelling circumstances Withdrawal without penalty Cross institutional study Unique Student Identifier (USI) Fees and other costs Payment methods Transcripts and documents Assessment and grades Exams Assessment timetable Deferred exams Grades Review of results Academic integrity Academic misconduct and how to avoid it Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen-AI) guide for students and staff Casual Room Bookings Services and support Bond Connect Academic Skills Centre Student Affairs and Service Quality Bond Business School Bond University College Attendance requirements Faculty of Health Sciences & Medicine Faculty of Law ​Indigenous student support Indigenous Student Success Program Nyombil Indigenous Support Centre International student support Medical and health services Student counselling Accessibility and inclusion Accessibility resources Feedback and questions University security Escape | Hide | Tell Emergency contacts Career Development Centre About the Career Development Centre Careers information for all our current students Employers and Industry Global experiences Graduates and alumni Verification of qualifications What's On Preventing and responding to gender-based violence Wellbeing services Student Wellbeing Advisors JP/Commissioner for Declarations service LGBTIQ+ services and support Campus life Bond University Student Association Student clubs Faculty Student Associations Bond University Business Students' Association Health and Sport Sciences Student Association (HSA) Medical Students Society of Bond University (MSSBU) Law Student Association Society & Design Student Association Club events Student events Students living on campus Sports Centre Smoke-free campus Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy (Teaching Focused) Start of main\n      content. Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy (Teaching Focused) Part-time 0.6 FTE, Fixed term for 2 years Reference number: 201393609 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university’, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Join an innovative Occupational Therapy discipline and make a meaningful impact in your field. Inspire the next generation of occupational therapists through contemporary, practice-focused education Teach in world-class, purpose-built facilities designed to enhance learning and clinical Occupational Therapy practice Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# Annual leave loading for continuing and fixed term Academic staff Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependants# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# Bond University is seeking an enthusiastic and experienced Occupational Therapist Academic to join our Occupational Therapy discipline as an Assistant Professor (Level A) or Associate Professor (Level B), Teaching Focused, on a part-time (0.6 FTE), two-year fixed-term appointment. This exciting opportunity will contribute to the delivery and ongoing development of Bond University’s Master of Occupational Therapy and Professional Doctor of Occupational Therapy programs, working alongside a passionate team of academics, clinicians and industry professionals committed to excellence and innovation in Occupational Therapy education. Our Master of Occupational Therapy is distinguished by its unique blend of case-based learning, practical application and more than 1,000 hours of practice-based education. Students gain experience across a broad range of clinical contexts and have opportunities to collaborate with community and industry partners through innovative research and industry projects. In this role, you will contribute to teaching across the breadth of Occupational Therapy, with emphasis aligned to your area of clinical and/or academic expertise. You will also support practical and case-based learning, contribute to practice education, and supervise clinical, industry and/or research activities undertaken by Occupational Therapy students. Our programs are accredited by the Occupational Therapy Council of Australia and the World Federation of Occupational Therapists (WFOT) and accreditation by ACOTE in the United States, reflecting our commitment to excellence in OT education and international recognition. About the person We are looking for passionate and driven Occupational Therapists who are registered (or eligible for registration) with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra). Ideal candidates will hold a Doctoral qualification and bring a proven track record of excellence in effective teaching, learning, scholarship, appropriate to the level of appointment. For the Associate Professor role, we are seeking candidates who demonstrate strong leadership, management, and team-building capabilities to inspire and support both staff and students. Salary details The salary for this position will be negotiated commensurate with skills, qualifications, and experience.  Salary packaging options are available.  The level of appointment will be determined by the Selection Panel. Associate Professor (Level B) in Occupational Therapy: The salary for this 0.6 FTE position commences at $103,918 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Full-time Equivalent is $173,197.62 per annum plus 12% superannuation. Assistant Professor (Level A) in Occupational Therapy: The salary for this 0.6 FTE position commences at $99,006.58 per annum, plus 12% superannuation.  Full-time Equivalent is $165,010.96 per annum plus 12% superannuation. This position is based at The Bond Institute of Health and Sport, Robina , located in the Robina Health precinct. A purpose-built teaching and training facility featuring contemporary clinical and teaching environments. Occupational Therapy students have access to specialised facilities including the Work Play Lab, Activities of Daily Living Lab with an independent living environment, paediatric facilities, and the Bond University Health and Wellness Clinic, providing rich opportunities for practical and authentic learning. Some travel between Bond University locations is required. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Professor Tawanda Machingura, Head of OT Program at [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. PD - Associate Professor (Level B) PD - Assistant Professor (Level A) Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11.59pm, Sunday 25 October 2026. Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Employment Contract (BEC). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 25th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twit"
