and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Be part of a forward-thinking occupational therapy academic team with a passion for teaching and mentoring students. Contribute to a global program accredited by leading bodies internationally. Engage in a dynamic and supportive teaching environment. Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# Bond University’s Occupational Therapy (OT) discipline is looking for qualified and experienced candidates to teach to our Postgraduate OT programs. We are seeking a variety of clinical expertise across the full scope of occupational therapy practice. Our OT Discipline offers students an innovative Master of Occupational Therapy and a newly established Professional Doctor of Occupational Therapy. Both programs are accredited by the Occupational Therapy Council of Australia and the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE) in the United States and approved by the World Federation of Occupational Therapy. Casual Academics are casual teaching focused positions and include all aspects of subject delivery including clinical supervision; preparing high quality subject and learning support materials; conducting face to face teaching; being available for consultation with students; designing and marking assessments; finalising grades; and undertaking administrative duties related to teaching and learning. These positions are available on an ‘as- needed’ basis to meet academic teaching requirements for the Occupational Therapy discipline. About the person We are looking for candidates to have the following: A master’s degree or higher qualification in a relevant field such as Occupational Therapy Full registration as an Occupational Therapist with AHPRA Substantial experience in Occupational Therapy i.e. Clinical background/experience in the following clinical OT practice areas: Ergonomics/ Work Rehabilitation/ Return to Work/ Vocational Rehabilitation, Neurorehabilitation, Indigenous Health or Mental Health. A commitment to high quality teaching and learning. Excellent interpersonal, communication and collaboration skills, including an ability to engage effectively with students. Skills in digital technologies and information systems Availability to teach on campus and/or Clinical practice supervision Salary details Applicants will be remunerated in accordance with the Bond University Casual Academic pay scales. Please note, that hours for these roles are casual in nature and may vary depending on the operational requirements of the faculty. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Dr. Tawanda Machingura, Head of Occupational Therapy on 07 5595 0176 or [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria . Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via HR Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Thursday 31 December 2026. Please note, the successful applicant will be required to produce a certified copy of their highest qualification received prior to commencement of duty. Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Employment Contract (BEC). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 31st December 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
