d Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Talent Acquisition Officer Start of main\n      content. Talent Acquisition Officer Full time, Fixed Term Appointment for 2 years Reference number: 201405316 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Love the details? Help deliver a seamless recruitment experience Use your strong administrative skills to support hiring across the University Create positive candidate experiences through every stage of hiring Talent Acquisition Officer People & Talent Office Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# Join the People and Talent team at Bond University and play a vital role in supporting the University's day-to-day recruitment operations. As the Talent Acquisition Officer, you will be the organisational backbone of the recruitment function, ensuring recruitment activities are coordinated efficiently, accurately and professionally across the employee lifecycle. From advertising roles and scheduling interviews to managing candidate communications and general administration, your attention to detail will help deliver a seamless recruitment experience. This is a highly administrative and process-focused role suited to someone who enjoys working in a fast-paced environment, managing multiple priorities and keeping information organised and up to date. You will be responsible for maintaining recruitment records and systems, coordinating recruitment logistics, supporting hiring managers and candidates, and ensuring recruitment processes are completed accurately and in line with University requirements. Working closely with the Talent Acquisition Lead and Talent Acquisition Advisor, you will contribute to a positive candidate experience by providing timely communication, professional support and exceptional customer service at every stage of the recruitment journey. Your ability to build strong relationships, manage details and proactively support recruitment activities will be key to your success. About the person You are a highly organised and customer-focused professional who takes pride in delivering accurate, timely and professional support. The ideal applicant will have the following: A bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant experience. Experience in recruitment administration, HR support or a similar coordination role. Strong administrative and organisational skills with exceptional attention to detail. A commitment to delivering outstanding candidate and stakeholder experiences. The ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Strong written and verbal communication skills and confidence working with a range of stakeholders. If you enjoy keeping processes running smoothly and providing exceptional support behind the scenes, we'd love to hear from you. Salary details The salary range for this full-time position is $74,096.61 to $80,450.93 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. The offer will be commensurate with relevant skills, qualifications and experience. Please note: The fixed term of this employment contract will be for two years, with twelve months' probation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Annelize Oosthuizen, Talent Acquisition Lead at [email protected] or 07-5595 1121. Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Sunday, 18 October 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 18th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
