Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Executive Officer, Committees Start of main\n      content. Executive Officer, Committees Full-time, Fixed Term for up to 2 years (Part-time appointments available at 0.8 FTE) Reference number: 201402501 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Play a key role in supporting positive student outcomes Experience a dynamic role encompassing a wide range of tasks Fantastic benefits package and great Gold Coast location Executive Officer, Committees Office of the Registrar Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# Join Bond University as an Executive Officer, Committees and play a pivotal role in supporting the University's academic governance framework. Working within the Academic Secretariat, you will provide high-level executive and secretariat support to key academic governance committees, helping to ensure effective decision-making and the delivery of exceptional outcomes for students and the broader University community. This is a varied and rewarding role where you'll coordinate committee operations from end to end, including managing schedules, preparing agendas and papers, attending meetings, recording minutes, tracking actions, and maintaining governance records. You'll also contribute to the administration of student appeals and disciplinary processes, providing professional support while managing sensitive matters with discretion, impartiality, and integrity. Partnering with senior academics, committee chairs, students, and professional staff, you'll be a trusted advisor on committee procedures and governance requirements while contributing to continuous improvement initiatives across the Academic Secretariat. About the person We're seeking a highly organised and professional administrator who thrives in a fast-paced environment and enjoys working with a broad range of stakeholders. You bring outstanding attention to detail, excellent written communication skills, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining accuracy and confidentiality. To be successful in this role, you will have: Relevant tertiary qualifications and demonstrated experience in executive, committee, or secretariat support Strong organisational and coordination skills, including experience preparing agendas, papers, minutes, and tracking actions Exceptional written communication and document management capabilities The ability to build effective working relationships with senior stakeholders and work collaboratively within a team Sound judgement, discretion, and the ability to manage confidential and sensitive matters professionally Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Teams, Word, and Excel A proactive approach, with the ability to work independently and adapt to changing priorities Experience supporting governance committees within a university or similarly regulated environment will be highly regarded, as will an understanding of governance frameworks, policy interpretation, and compliance requirements. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $99,108.89 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Please note: The fixed term of this employment contract will be for up to two years, with twelve months' probation. The prospect of conversion to a continuing employment contract will be discussed at the end of the contract term. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Natasha Kollosche, Manager - Academic Secretariat on 07 5595 2518 or [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm Sunday 25 th October, 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at any time during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 25th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
