ies Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Program Manager, Transformation CoLab Start of main\n      content. Program Manager, Transformation CoLab Part-time {0.5FTE}, Fixed Term for up to 12 months (Parental Leave Cover) Reference number: 184675604 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Make a real impact on students’ university journeys and future careers. Build industry partnerships that connect students with real-world experience. Enjoy a varied, part-time role combining student support and industry engagement. Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# As the principal point of contact for students across the two Transformation Programs, you will guide their progress from entry through to graduation, helping them understand program requirements, navigate study pathways and access the support they need to succeed. A key focus of the role is developing and maintaining strong industry partnerships to create relevant and rewarding workplace immersion experiences. You will oversee the placement process from identifying suitable opportunities and matching students with host organisations through to coordinating arrangements, monitoring progress and resolving any issues. Alongside student support and industry engagement, you will contribute to the day-to-day coordination of the programs, working collaboratively with academic and professional teams to ensure a positive and consistent student experience. Key responsibilities include: Student support: Guide students through their studies, providing personalised advice and monitoring academic progression. Industry partnerships: Build and maintain relationships with industry partners to create meaningful workplace immersion opportunities. Placement coordination: Manage student placements, including matching students with hosts and overseeing placement arrangements. Program coordination: Support the effective delivery and continuous improvement of both programs, working collaboratively with University teams. Stakeholder engagement: Contribute to industry networking, student recruitment and promotional activities About the person You’re a proactive, organised and relationship-focused professional who enjoys supporting others, building industry connections and coordinating multiple priorities. To be successful, you will bring: A completed university degree or equivalent, with significant relevant experience. Experience in higher education or training environments. Proven ability to develop industry partnerships and coordinate workplace learning or placement opportunities. Strong communication, networking and stakeholder engagement skills. Excellent organisational, administrative and problem-solving skills. The ability to work independently, exercise sound judgement and collaborate effectively with diverse teams. Strong computer literacy and experience with common office applications and databases. Experience with university systems and a current Australian driver’s licence would be advantageous. Salary details The salary for this {0.5 FTE} position commences at $58,097 per annum (Full-time Equivalent is $116,195 per annum) plus 12% superannuation per annum. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Jeff Brand, Deputy Provost Education on 07 5595 2511 or [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Monday 26 October 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 26th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
