ld Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Position Reference No: 201393410 About the Position: Bond University is seeking experienced Executive Assistants to join our Casual Administration Register (CAR), supporting senior leaders across the University. The register is used to fill short-term and fixed-term opportunities, including executive leave cover and periods of increased operational demand. Executive Assistants play a critical role in enabling senior leaders to operate effectively, providing trusted, high-level support within fast-paced and complex environments. Responsibilities may include: End-to-end executive office support, including diary and inbox management Coordination of meetings, committees, travel, events, and executive priorities Preparation of high-quality correspondence, reports, briefs, agendas, and minutes Management of sensitive and confidential information with discretion Coordination of events, projects, and engagement with internal and external stakeholders Financial and administrative support, including budget tracking and approvals Please note: This is an expression of interest register. Candidates will be contacted as suitable opportunities arise that align with their skills, experience, and availability. About the person We are seeking professionals who bring: Proven experience providing high-level executive or senior administrative support Strong judgement, discretion, and confidence engaging with senior stakeholders Experience supporting complex offices, projects, events, or financial administration Exceptional organisation skills and the ability to manage competing priorities Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office and administrative systems A collaborative, adaptable approach and interest in working within a university environment Contract length can vary from a casual appointment with an hourly rate to a shorter fixed term assignment. Salary details Hourly rates will generally vary between $56.05 - $64.10 per hour plus 12% super, depending on the level of skill and expertise required to undertake the role. Additional information Position related enquiries can be directed to the Talent team at [email protected] . Please see below for information on how to apply. Application and submission details Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University. Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy APPLY NOW Applications close: 1st November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
